        "narrative": "The quietest week of flow in the layer and the biggest change in the desk's positioning. TSMC appears in the feed only in passing \u2014 the Amkor ten-year packaging agreement, the NVIDIA deal, an aside about how the ticker is pronounced \u2014 while its own disclosure did the talking: first-half revenue up 35.6% year on year with June alone up 67.9%.\n\nThe structural point that matters for the whole map is that the advanced-packaging squeeze is loosening. Industry reporting has the CoWoS supply-demand gap narrowing from roughly 20% to 10% by the end of 2026, with capacity heading toward about 200,000 wafers a month by end-2027. That is why scarcity on this map keeps migrating upstream into lasers and substrates rather than staying in packaging.\n\nGlobalFoundries and Intel are unchanged and unmentioned. The CHIPS silicon-photonics award remains GlobalFoundries' whole case, and Intel's disclosed 14A schedule still puts risk production in 2027 and volume in 2028.",
