        "narrative": "AMD's quarter answered the question this desk actually has about the layer. Data-centre revenue was $6.7bn, up 107% year on year, and the 10-Q attributes it to EPYC processors and MI350-series parts \u2014 not to MI450. Helios entered production with shipments starting at the end of the third quarter, and the first gigawatt of the announced Anthropic deployment begins in the first half of 2027.\n\nSo the co-packaged optics read-through the feed keeps drawing from AMD's rack-scale roadmap to the laser suppliers is a 2027 event at the earliest, and the 2027 doubling is already the consensus case at the current price. That is three quarters of carry with nothing to prove it in between.\n\nNVIDIA barely features this week beyond breadth lists, and its position is unchanged: management's own guidance is that supply stays constrained through the entire life of Vera Rubin, which is the demand hub underwriting the upstream bottleneck thesis. The offsetting fact is concentration \u2014 data centre is roughly 92% of revenue, sold to a handful of buyers.",
