        "ticker": "COHR",
        "stance": "watch",
        "previousStance": "watch",
        "view": "Up roughly 71% in a week on a thesis that is still, in this corpus, entirely by association \u2014 no dedicated Coherent post with numbers attached. Fiscal Q4 lands 12 August against a $1.91-2.05bn guide. The seats found the structural objection: non-GAAP gross margin was 39.6% last quarter, well below the component pure-plays, because industrial and telecom dilute the datacenter mix. And the PM seat's warning is the one to hold \u2014 a meaningful part of this move discounts a proposed US ban on new Chinese transceivers that exists only as a draft with nothing published in the Federal Register.",
        "execution": "No dedicated action, and specifically do not buy the ban. LITE carries the same shortage at higher purity with disclosed numbers. If Coherent earns a position it will be on its own datacenter segment math in Wednesday's print, not on the sector's tape.",
        "changesMind": "Coherent sizing its datacenter segment separately with margins to match, which would make the conglomerate discount an opportunity rather than a reason to own LITE instead.",
