        "title": "The CPO read-through has no AMD behind it",
        "dek": "Enters Core on score. The desk's interest is co-packaged optics adoption, and that rests on channel checks, not disclosure.",
        "publishedAt": "2026-08-03T00:00:00Z",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-03T00:00:00Z",
        "rating": "watch",
        "sections": [
          {
            "heading": "Snapshot",
            "body": "$AMD enters Core coverage on mention volume, largely as the presumed first customer for co-packaged optics among the [[accelerators]]."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Thesis",
            "body": "If AMD commits to CPO for Helios scale-up networking, it converts the [[photonics]] laser suppliers from a thematic bet into a scheduled one, with [[aaoi]] and [[sive]] the named beneficiaries."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Why own it",
            "body": "Independently of the optics narrative, the accelerator business is compounding: Q1 data centre revenue of $5.8bn was up 57%, with Q2 guided to roughly $11.2bn plus or minus $300m, about 46% growth at the midpoint."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Risks",
            "body": "The CPO adoption claim traces to channel checks and a Rosenblatt note, not to any AMD disclosure. Helios and MI450 ship in the second half of 2026 on pluggable optics, with co-packaged optics described as a future-generation option \u2014 which puts the read-through in 2027 at the earliest.\n\nQ2 results land 4 August against a guide already embedding 46% growth, making the near term a binary on execution."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Bottom line",
            "body": "Watch. Do not take a position into the print, and do not own AMD as a proxy for the photonics thesis \u2014 if AMD is worth owning it is as an accelerator business on its own numbers."
          }
        ],
