        "sections": [
          {
            "heading": "Snapshot",
            "body": "$AXTI leaves the verdict roster this week on score, ranking 25th. Its last recorded desk stance was watch and no position was ever suggested."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Thesis",
            "body": "AXT supplies the indium phosphide substrates that [[lite]] and [[cohr]] turn into lasers, which makes it the upstream chokepoint of the chokepoint \u2014 one link further up than the [[photonics]] names the desk owns."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Why own it",
            "body": "The long-term supplier agreement with Lumentum reserves a minimum annual indium phosphide commitment through 31 December 2031 and supports additional capacity if required. Being paid in advance to reserve capacity is what a genuine bottleneck looks like."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Risks",
            "body": "The agreement is two deposits of $43.5m, $87m in total, with the second only in calendar 2028. Both operate as shipment credits offset against future invoices, not fees \u2014 the cash arrives years before the revenue does.\n\nNo wafer volumes, pricing or capacity figures are disclosed, so the scale of the reservation cannot be sized from the filing. Concentration also rises: the small group of laser makers reserving the capacity are the only buyers of the output."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Bottom line",
            "body": "Leaves coverage without a position ever having been taken, which is the right outcome for a name whose entire attraction was a cash line that turns out to be deferred revenue. The exposure is better held through [[lite]]."
          }
        ],
