        "note": "Applied Optoelectronics is the high-beta datacom optics position in the book \u2014 the name whose valuation case has always rested on a forward revenue rate rather than current earnings. The 800G ramp itself is real and company-confirmed: Q1 revenue was a record $151.1m, up 51%, with Q2 shipments guided at nearly four times Q1 levels.\n\nOn 3 August 2026 the desk stepped the stance from accumulate to watch. The $471m monthly rate anchoring the bull case \u2014 about $5.6bn annualised from H2 2027 \u2014 is roughly five times the run-rate management guides to, with Q2 at $180-198m and the full year around $1.1bn. It circulates in the [[photonics]] discussion as though it were the company's own estimate. Q2 is also guided to non-GAAP EPS between -$0.03 and +$0.03, so the 'one times forward revenue' cheapness describes a top line that currently earns nothing.\n\nThe trigger back to accumulate is management guiding toward the rate the thesis assumes, or a named CPO customer with committed volume \u2014 see [[amd]], where that read-through is still inference rather than schedule.",
