        "note": "Nebius is the [[neoclouds]] position \u2014 the way to own AI compute demand without owning a hyperscaler or a chip designer. The operating execution is visible and on schedule: up to 1.2GW of power and land secured for an owned Pennsylvania site, and more than 3GW expected under contract by year-end. For a neocloud, energised capacity is the binding constraint and it is being cleared ahead of the revenue.\n\nOn 3 August 2026 the desk stepped the stance from accumulate to watch. Q1 revenue was $399.0m, annualising near $1.6bn against a full-year target of $3-3.4bn, so almost the entire guide sits in the second half. Capex plans run an order of magnitude above revenue, which makes the terms of the next capital raise a larger determinant of the equity return than GPU demand is.\n\nAccumulate implied the risk being underwritten was demand. It is not \u2014 it is financing. Q2 results on 12 August are the next test. [[iren]] entered coverage the same week with better counterparties and the same unresolved funding question.",
